  "identity": {
    "playing_style": "Identity is in transition: Arne Slot's 4-2-3-1 possession-and-press model won the 2024/25 title but collapsed to 5th (60 pts, 53 conceded, 12 defeats) in 2025/26 despite GBP 440m+ of signings, and Slot was dismissed on 30 May 2026. Andoni Iraola (appointed 4 June 2026, two-year deal) brings the high-intensity, man-marking press and relentlessly vertical attacking that took Bournemouth to 6th; he is expected to keep a 4-2-3-1 with short build-up from the keeper and direct play when pressed. The rebuilt front line (Barcola, Muñoz, Wirtz, Isak, Ekitike, Gakpo) suits a transition-heavy game; Salah, Konaté and Robertson all left.",
    "principles": [
      "data-led recruitment (research department under FSG)",
      "buy under-25 with resale value; occasional marquee exception",
      "wage discipline relative to revenue",
      "'This means more' - community and Hillsborough legacy",
      "Academy pathway (Bradley, Nyoni, Ngumoha)"
    ],
    "club_character": "US private ownership (FSG) with a data-driven, financially prudent model; intense but supportive Anfield atmosphere; club leaning on a sporting-director structure (Richard Hughes, Michael Edwards as FSG CEO of football) rather than a single manager.",
    "ownership": "Fenway Sports Group (private, US) with Dynasty Equity minority stake",
    "political_and_social_context": "Club and supporters publicly opposed the 2021 European Super League and withdrew within 48 hours after fan protests; long-standing institutional campaigning on Hillsborough justice and against The Sun newspaper; fan groups (Spirit of Shankly) have formal consultation with the board; public statements on ticket pricing and UEFA final security (Paris 2022).",
    "languages": [
      "en",
      "nl",
      "fr",
      "de",
      "es"
    ],
    "wage_structure": "hierarchical but capped relative to revenue; performance-linked bonuses",
    "transfer_policy": "Data-led, under-25 focus with premium spent on elite talent in 2025 and 2026 (Wirtz, Isak in 2025; Barcola ~EUR 123m, Jacquet up to GBP 60m, Muñoz EUR 40m in 2026); accepts free-agent exits of ageing stars (Salah, Konaté, Robertson) rather than long renewals",
    "injury_management_reputation": "Publicly discussed: recurring hamstring problems (Jota, Konate) and Alisson's fitness were themes in 2025/26; Barcola signing partly justified by attacking depth issues."
  },
